// Title: HackTool - Mimikatz Kirbi File Creation
// Sigma ID: 9e099d99-44c2-42b6-a6d8-54c3545cab29
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), David ANDRE
// Date: 2021-11-08 | Modified: 2024-06-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1558
// Description: Detects the creation of files created by mimikatz such as ".kirbi", "mimilsa.log", etc.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://cobalt.io/blog/kerberoast-attack-techniques
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2019/10/21/persistence-security-support-provider/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_hktl_mimikatz_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith ".kirbi" or FolderPath endswith "mimilsa.log"
